{
{{IF:OPUSPLAN}}  "model": "opusplan",
  "fallbackModel": ["default"],
  "permissions": {
    "_comment": "A deny list is a SPELLING list. The Read rules stop the Read tool on the conventional secret-bearing names and on no others: .env, .env.local, .env.*.local, .env.production, .env.development, .env.staging and .env.test, so the .env.example the stamp writes stays readable and a secret file named any other way is not covered. The Bash deny for reading environment files names the same files, so the .env.example stays readable from the shell too, and it stops one Bash spelling and nothing else: less, head, tail, sed, a $(<.env) expansion, a source or a grep read the same file and are not listed, and the scope hook watches the file-writing tools, not Bash. This key is where the note lives because it is what the harness tolerates: measured 2026-09-07 on Claude Code 2.1.259, a _comment key here left every rule in force, and a // comment made the file unreadable and silently dropped every rule in it. A key a newer Claude Code adds to this file can cost the whole file on an older one: 2.1.281's scalar attribution: false makes an older harness skip the file, these rules and the four session hooks with it, while its content still reads as wired. Nothing Setlist ships writes such a key, and the git hooks refuse regardless. The rules have a version floor: Claude Code 2.1.289 fixed a deny or ask rule being skipped under sandbox auto-allow when the command carries a variable-assignment prefix, so below 2.1.289 read the ask rules in front of git reset --hard and rm -rf as advisory (not reproduced headless at 2.1.288 in four spellings, 2026-10-07; the floor is the changelog's). The bypass deny's entry carries onFailure block, which has a floor of its own: from Claude Code 2.1.295 a bypass deny that times out or cannot start blocks the command instead of letting it through (measured 2026-10-14 at 2.1.299), and below 2.1.295 the key is ignored, the hook still runs and every rule in this file stays in force (measured at 2.1.292), so there a failed bypass deny is a skipped one. The scope hook and the Stop hook carry no such key: the scope hook is advice, and the key has no effect on Stop hooks.",
    "deny": [
      "Read(.env)",
      "Read(.env.local)",
      "Read(.env.*.local)",
      "Read(.env.production)",
      "Read(.env.development)",
      "Read(.env.staging)",
      "Read(.env.test)",
      "Bash(cat .env)",
      "Bash(cat .env *)",
      "Bash(cat .env.local)",
      "Bash(cat .env.local *)",
      "Bash(cat .env.*.local)",
      "Bash(cat .env.*.local *)",
      "Bash(cat .env.production)",
      "Bash(cat .env.production *)",
      "Bash(cat .env.development)",
      "Bash(cat .env.development *)",
      "Bash(cat .env.staging)",
      "Bash(cat .env.staging *)",
      "Bash(cat .env.test)",
      "Bash(cat .env.test *)"
    ],
    "ask": [
      "Bash(git push*)",
      "Bash(git reset --hard*)",
      "Bash(git push --force*)",
      "Bash(rm -rf*)"
    ]
  },
  "hooks": {
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": "Write|Edit|MultiEdit|NotebookEdit",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/.claude/hooks/scope-hook.sh",
            "timeout": 120
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "Bash",
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/.claude/hooks/bypass-deny.sh",
            "timeout": 300,
            "onFailure": "block"
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/.claude/hooks/regrounding-hook.sh",
            "timeout": 60
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          {
            "type": "command",
            "command": "\"$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR\"/.claude/hooks/stop-hook.sh",
            "timeout": 60
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
